---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CalculatorCard from '../components/CalculatorCard.astro';
import { calculators, categories } from '../data/calculators.js';
import { absoluteSiteUrl } from '../data/site.js';

const description = 'Accurate, fast online calculators for finance, health, math, dates, education, and everyday life.';
const homeUrl = absoluteSiteUrl(import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'ClearCalc Tools', url: homeUrl, description },
    {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      name: 'ClearCalc calculators',
      itemListElement: calculators.map((item, index) => ({
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: index + 1,
        name: item.title,
        url: absoluteSiteUrl(`/calculators/${item.slug}/`)
      }))
    }
  ]
};
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify(schema).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<Layout title="Free Online Calculators | ClearCalc Tools" description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
  <section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">FREE • FAST • PRIVATE</span><h1>Calculate with confidence.</h1><p>Clear answers for money, health, school, and everyday decisions. No signup required.</p><a class="button" href="#calculators">Explore calculators</a></div><div class="hero-panel"><span>Quick calculation</span><strong>Simple inputs.</strong><strong>Clear results.</strong><strong>Useful explanations.</strong></div></section>
  <section class="trust"><span>✓ No account</span><span>✓ Mobile friendly</span><span>✓ Transparent formulas</span></section>
  <section id="calculators" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">CALCULATOR LIBRARY</span><h2>Popular calculators</h2></div><p>Choose a tool and get an answer in seconds.</p></div>
    {categories.map((category) => {
      const categoryId = category.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
      return <div class="category-section" id={categoryId}><h3 class="category-title">{category}</h3><div class="card-grid">{calculators.filter((item) => item.category === category).map((item) => <CalculatorCard item={item} />)}</div></div>;
    })}
  </section>
  <section class="content-band"><h2>Designed to make numbers easier</h2><p>Every ClearCalc tool focuses on one job, shows the formula it uses, and runs in your browser. Nothing you type is sent to a ClearCalc account. Results are estimates. For an important money or health decision, compare the result with a qualified professional and with the lender, school, or clinician who has your actual terms.</p><p>The <a href={`${base}calculators/mortgage-calculator/`}>mortgage payment calculator</a> and the <a href={`${base}calculators/loan-calculator/`}>loan payment calculator</a> both use standard monthly amortization, with taxes and fees left out so the interest math stays visible. The <a href={`${base}calculators/compound-interest-calculator/`}>compound interest calculator</a> projects a balance from a starting amount and end-of-month deposits. Health tools cover <a href={`${base}calculators/bmi-calculator/`}>adult BMI</a> from kilograms and centimeters and a <a href={`${base}calculators/calorie-calculator/`}>maintenance-calorie estimate</a> from the Mifflin–St Jeor equation for men or women. Everyday math includes a <a href={`${base}calculators/percentage-calculator/`}>percentage calculator</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/tip-calculator/`}>tip split</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/discount-calculator/`}>percent-off sale price</a>, and a <a href={`${base}calculators/length-converter/`}>length converter</a> from meters to feet, inches, yards, or kilometers. Date tools count an <a href={`${base}calculators/age-calculator/`}>exact age</a> or the <a href={`${base}calculators/date-difference-calculator/`}>days between two dates</a>. Work and pay includes a <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>2026/27 take-home pay calculator</a> for employees in England, Wales, and Northern Ireland. The <a href={`${base}calculators/gpa-calculator/`}>GPA calculator</a> averages four unweighted grades on a 4.0 scale, and the <a href={`${base}calculators/final-exam-grade-calculator/`}>final exam grade calculator</a> solves for the score a weighted final needs. Home projects include a <a href={`${base}calculators/concrete-slab-calculator/`}>concrete slab calculator</a> that turns feet and inches into bags and cubic yards.</p><p>Five later tools answer questions the earlier pages leave open. The <a href={`${base}calculators/new-york-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 New York paycheck calculator</a> adds New York State tax and, when you ask for it, New York City resident tax. The <a href={`${base}calculators/alberta-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Alberta take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 Alberta brackets, CPP, and EI, with no provincial health premium. The <a href={`${base}calculators/nsw-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>NSW stamp duty calculator</a> applies 2026/27 New South Wales transfer duty, including the first home buyer concession. The <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-student-loan-repayment-calculator/`}>UK student loan repayment calculator</a> estimates a 2026/27 Plan 1, Plan 2, Plan 4, Plan 5, or postgraduate deduction, which the England take-home page does not subtract. The <a href={`${base}calculators/room-paint-calculator/`}>room paint calculator</a> turns a rectangular room into gallons. The <a href={`${base}calculators/date-difference-calculator/`}>day counter</a> still includes weekends: calendar year 2026 has 261 weekdays, 52 Saturdays, and 52 Sundays, and the elapsed count from 1 January to 31 December remains 364.</p><p>Pay calculators are split by the tax system they use. The <a href={`${base}calculators/texas-paycheck-calculator/`}>Texas paycheck calculator</a> and the <a href={`${base}calculators/florida-paycheck-calculator/`}>Florida paycheck calculator</a> estimate 2026 federal income tax, Social Security, and Medicare, with a state income tax line of zero. The <a href={`${base}calculators/california-paycheck-calculator/`}>California paycheck calculator</a> adds 2026 California income tax and State Disability Insurance. The <a href={`${base}calculators/washington-paycheck-calculator/`}>Washington paycheck calculator</a> keeps state income tax at $0 and subtracts 2026 Paid Leave and WA Cares. The <a href={`${base}calculators/scotland-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Scotland take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026/27 Scottish income tax bands. The <a href={`${base}calculators/ontario-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Ontario take-home pay calculator</a> uses 2026 federal and Ontario rates, CPP, and EI. The <a href={`${base}calculators/british-columbia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>British Columbia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 B.C. brackets, including the 5.60% first rate and the tax reduction. The <a href={`${base}calculators/australia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Australia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026–27 resident rates, the low income tax offset, and the Medicare levy. The <a href={`${base}calculators/england-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>England stamp duty calculator</a> applies residential SDLT, including first-time buyer relief and the additional-dwelling rates. Work tools also include an <a href={`${base}calculators/hourly-to-salary-calculator/`}>hourly to salary calculator</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/overtime-pay-calculator/`}>weekly overtime pay calculator</a>, and a <a href={`${base}calculators/401k-contribution-calculator/`}>2026 401(k) contribution calculator</a>. The <a href={`${base}calculators/rent-affordability-calculator/`}>rent affordability calculator</a> compares rent with 30% of gross income.</p><p>Another set of tools answers a narrower question than the page beside it. The <a href={`${base}calculators/illinois-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Illinois paycheck calculator</a> keeps the federal brackets and then applies the 4.95% Illinois rate after a $2,925 exemption, which is a different subtraction from the New York brackets or from a state line of zero. The <a href={`${base}calculators/manitoba-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Manitoba take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 Manitoba brackets, 10.8%, 12.75%, and 17.4%, with the $15,780 basic personal amount, on top of the same federal, CPP, and EI figures as Alberta. The <a href={`${base}calculators/victoria-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Victoria stamp duty calculator</a> applies Victorian land transfer duty, including the first home buyer concession through $750,000 and the 8% foreign purchaser additional duty. The <a href={`${base}calculators/us-business-days-calculator/`}>US business days calculator</a> counts inclusive weekdays and can remove the 11 federal holidays. For 2026 that leaves 250 business days, against 261 weekdays and against the 364 elapsed days from 1 January to 31 December on the day counter. The <a href={`${base}calculators/mulch-calculator/`}>mulch calculator</a> turns a bed measured in feet, and a depth in inches, into cubic yards and 2 or 3 cubic foot bags. A 10 by 20 foot bed at 3 inches is 25 of the 2 cubic foot bags, which is not the bag count on the concrete page.</p><p>Five more tools fill gaps those pages leave. The <a href={`${base}calculators/pennsylvania-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Pennsylvania paycheck calculator</a> applies the 3.07% state tax to wages before a 401(k), then a local earned income tax rate you type and a flat local services tax. At $65,000, single, with a 1% local rate and $52, the two-week headline is $1,988.85. The <a href={`${base}calculators/saskatchewan-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Saskatchewan take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets, 10.5%, 12.5%, and 14.5%, and a $20,381 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,389.11, between Alberta and Manitoba on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/queensland-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Queensland stamp duty calculator</a> follows the Queensland Revenue Office scales, including $6,555 of transfer duty on a $730,000 established first home. The <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-working-days-calculator/`}>UK working days calculator</a> counts inclusive weekdays and can remove bank holidays. England and Wales have 253 working days in 2026, against 250 US business days and against 261 weekdays. The <a href={`${base}calculators/gravel-calculator/`}>gravel calculator</a> turns the same 10 by 20 foot, 3 inch area the mulch page uses into 2.625 short tons of dry gravel at 105 lb per cubic foot.</p><p>Five further tools answer a different statute or a different unit. The <a href={`${base}calculators/ohio-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Ohio paycheck calculator</a> follows Ohio Revised Code 5747.02: no nonbusiness tax on the first $26,050 of Ohio taxable income, then $332 plus 2.75% of the excess, after a personal exemption. At $65,000, single, with one exemption and the school district and city rates left at zero, Ohio tax is $1,344.00 and the two-week headline is $2,040.90. The <a href={`${base}calculators/nova-scotia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Nova Scotia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets, starting at 8.79%, and a $11,932 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,208.02, which is $2,173.04 below Saskatchewan on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/scotland-lbtt-calculator/`}>Scotland LBTT calculator</a> applies residential Land and Buildings Transaction Tax, including first-time buyer relief of up to £600 and the 8% additional dwelling supplement. A £250,000 main home is £2,100, against £2,500 of SDLT on the England page. The <a href={`${base}calculators/canada-business-days-calculator/`}>Canada business days calculator</a> removes statutory holidays for Ontario, British Columbia, or Alberta. Ontario has 253 business days in 2026, British Columbia 250, and Alberta 252, against 261 weekdays. The <a href={`${base}calculators/5k-pace-calculator/`}>5K pace calculator</a> turns a finish time into minutes per kilometre and per mile. A 25:00 5K is 5:00 per kilometre and 8:02.8 per mile, which is not a calorie total.</p></section>
</Layout>
